WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.176
[lively conversation.
gavel bangs]

2
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.440
We need to vote - now.

3
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.856
And I urge you all to remember.

4
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.336
my father and every headmaster
before him

5
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.560
protected this school
and its legacy. tooth and nail.

6
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.416
-Bloody freezing out here.
-I know.

7
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.056
But we can't go in till that
stupid board meeting's over.

8
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.296
They were supposed to be done
by now.

9
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.096
Even the council agreed. before
the Planning Act was overridden.

10
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.040
We should not sell this land.

11
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.656
[murmurs]

12
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.016
OK. I really do think
we should wait.

13
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.896
The vote is split down the
middle. so Vincent's vote will matter.

14
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.240
The headmaster knows
the vote is due.

15
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.736
It's not our job
to wait for him.

16
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.296
What do you think.
deputy headmaster?

17
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.080
He's not answering his phone.

18
00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.096
Perhaps he's excluding himself.

19
00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.976
I doubt that. it's his proposal.

20
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.016
Oh. for heaven's sake.

21
00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.256
Let's take a 20-minute break.
then. but no longer.

22
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.640
-We've been here all evening.
-[grumbles]

23
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.040
The lights are still on.

24
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.600
[crows cawing]

25
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.240
What the hell is that?

26
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:28.840
[dripping]

27
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.960
No!

28
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.640
Hurry up and go!

29
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.040
[theme music]

30
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.056
You don't need to do anything.
all right?

31
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.256
Just be free for those two days.
I'll book it.

32
00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.456
[Lola] <i>Are you sure?
I have travel vouchers.</i>

33
00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.976
Will you just
let me surprise you?!

34
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.240
-[laughs]
<i>-OK.</i>

35
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.376
Gotta go. Lols. Chat later.

36
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.440
Oi! Reid!

37
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.440
[pacey. dramatic music]

38
00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.256
This isn't school.

39
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.520
I'm not scared of you
or your little gang.

40
00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.256
-Jesus! Bloody hell!
-Ow!

41
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.336
-What did you do that for?
-You were coming at me!

42
00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.696
-I wasn't coming at you.
-You were chasing me!

43
00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.056
-To ask for your help!
-Help?

44
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.040
Help with what?

45
00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.400
People think I'm a murderer.

46
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.440
I need you to clear my name.

47
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.720
Ow!

48
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.456
[sighs] Really. Fergus? Is this
a new approach to clients?

49
00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.256
He's not a client.

50
00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.616
He's probably just in trouble
with a drug dealer or something.

51
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.776
-You heard of St Bart's?
-Yeah. I've heard of it.

52
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:09.136
It's a boys' boarding school.
very exclusive.

53
00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.936
Yeah. an old friend of mine.
um...

54
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.856
Kevin Monroe
was the principal there.

55
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.496
Well. he passed ten years ago

56
00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.576
and I think he was replaced
by Vincent something?

57
00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:17.960
Quinn.

58
00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.056
Last week. he was thrown out
of the top floor.

59
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.176
-Oh. so you pushed him?
-No. I didn't.

60
00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.576
We'd a bit of beef.
He kept trying to expel me.

61
00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.456
Ooh. what do you mean expel you?
You're not in that school.

62
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.880
I am. Now.

63
00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.416
-I got a scholarship.
-Very impressive.

64
00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.216
There's no way you got in.
You're a bullying little shit.

65
00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.976
Well. from where I'm standing.
you're the one that clocked him.

66
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.136
He used to call me Weedy Reidy.

67
00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.136
Really? That's funny.
No. I mean... it's terrible.

68
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.376
Really. it's terrible.
It's terrible.

69
00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.416
Can you help me?

70
00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.840
Why do people think
that you killed him?

71
00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.456
I did some stupid shit.
all right?

72
00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.456
Just messing. like. but...

73
00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.256
I kept getting into trouble
with Mr Quinn.

74
00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.736
Mm-hm.

75
00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.840
So. when he died.
the police went straight for me.

76
00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.056
I was in me form room
when he died.

77
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.000
I didn't leave it.
I swear on me ma's life.

78
00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.560
I couldn't have killed him.

79
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.040
What?

80
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.736
[Charlie] From Jordan.
"Vincent Quinn."

81
00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.256
Bruising to indicate
he was pushed

82
00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.216
from the top floor of St Bart's.

83
00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.696
They were doing some renovations
so there was scaffolding.

84
00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.736
but he hit his head off
another balcony on the way down.

85
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.256
Instant death.
approximately 9:30pm.

86
00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.736
His spectacles were missing.
they found that odd.

87
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.616
He always wore them.

88
00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.016
They suspect they fell from
his face during the altercation

89
00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.896
"and the killer picked them up."

90
00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.336
Ah. Thanks. Jordan.

91
00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.880
-Crime scene pics.
-Hm.

92
00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.056
He left the school board meeting
at 9pm

93
00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.616
after receiving a call
on his mobile.

94
00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.976
The call came from the school's
internal phone system.

95
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.216
so they can't pin it down
to a specific phone.

96
00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.480
All the boys were
in their form rooms. allegedly.

97
00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.336
Well. he's unlikely to have left
an important board meeting

98
00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.416
to go and inspect construction
at that hour.

99
00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.616
Somebody obviously summoned him
to the top floor.

100
00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.496
Yeah. Derek.

101
00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.016
Well. that's not proven.

102
00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.656
but I would be inclined
to check on him closely.

103
00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.416
Kids these days. Ma.
they're a different breed.

104
00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.176
and it sounds like he had cause.

105
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.600
There'll be a memorial.
I think we should all go.

106
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.496
My old friend's daughter's
still involved in this school.

107
00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.840
We could ask questions without
deciding one way or the other.

108
00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.336
This is a time of great sadness.

109
00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.896
and while we are mourning now.

110
00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:51.840
we must remember that St Bart's
is not just a school.

111
00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.576
We are a community

112
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.400
-and we will support each other.
-It's Sherry Monroe. previous headmaster's daughter.

113
00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.960
I believe that's her husband.

114
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.360
We should mingle.

115
00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.776
[Sherry] My father was
very fond of you.

116
00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:22.656
[Harry] And I him.
He was a good soul.

117
00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.256
It's good to see that you're
still involved with the school.

118
00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.416
Oh. St Bart's is our family.

119
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.656
-My two sons go here.
-[hum of conversations]

120
00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.336
This school means
everything to us.

121
00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.600
It's a tragedy what happened.

122
00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.136
Did you like him?
Vincent. I mean.

123
00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.136
Of course.

124
00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.256
I heard there was a vote
taking place the night he died.

125
00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.600
-Is that true?
-Mm-hm.

126
00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:51.056
Vincent wanted to sell off
some of the school land.

127
00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.416
and he'd brought half
the teachers and board around.

128
00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:56.096
So. it was split
down the middle?

129
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.656
Mm-hm.

130
00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.960
Why did anyone
want to oppose it?

131
00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:03.336
That land had protected status.

132
00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.560
Even the council
acknowledged it.

133
00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.576
And it was used by the local
community. not just the school.

134
00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.496
And then. suddenly.
it was overturned

135
00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.296
and they decided to zone it
for houses.

136
00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.456
The area would lose a resource.
the school would be flanked.

137
00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.456
I mean. Vincent was like a dog
with a bone trying to sell.

138
00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.976
Yeah. we're friends of the family. It's
great to see how well-loved Vincent was.

139
00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.280
Yeah. Quinner. he was. er...
he was all right.

140
00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.200
It's not true what
they're saying. though. is it?

141
00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.280
That. er...

142
00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:38.896
[whispers]
That Derek pushed him?

143
00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.896
-Who's saying that?
-Everyone.

144
00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:45.800
What was the story
between him and. er... Quinner?

145
00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.096
Well. Derek. he was always
fronting up to him.

146
00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.776
And as head boy.
I tried to rein him in

147
00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.136
but they had a massive
blow-up that day.

148
00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.280
Hm.

149
00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.000
I heard Derek didn't leave
his form room that night.

150
00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.160
Did he say that?

151
00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.896
-So. you're in charge now?
-Acting head.

152
00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:15.096
Sherry tells me that your son
is a senior Guard.

153
00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.656
On sabbatical at the moment.

154
00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.976
Does he have any information
about this case?

155
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.136
It's just. the board doesn't
know what to do

156
00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.096
until the Guards charge Derek.

157
00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.936
Or not.

158
00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:31.816
He could sue the school if
we expel him during all of this.

159
00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.336
claim that we prejudged
the outcome.

160
00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.576
We have to be very careful. what
with him being a scholarship kid

161
00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.936
and the fact that he's...

162
00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.616
Poor? Disadvantaged?
Marginalised?

163
00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:46.856
Oh. that has nothing
to do with it!

164
00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:49.136
This school has always been
about equality

165
00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:51.576
and giving
the less well-off access.

166
00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.440
Derek has been
very welcome here.

167
00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:58.576
Even Vincent said the sale money
would go into more scholarships.

168
00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.256
Well. did you agree
with his plan?

169
00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.896
God. no!

170
00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.496
It's a terrible idea.
Putting profit over history?

171
00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.176
Well. if the vote
was contentious

172
00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.976
and I was the police.
I would be wondering

173
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.576
who was benefitting
from Vincent.

174
00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:15.120
the casting vote.
not being there?

175
00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:18.840
Look. everybody knows
that it was Derek.

176
00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.400
That's why we're so eager
to hear what the police think.

177
00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.256
I really think we should
just suspend him. Arthur.

178
00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:29.240
-It's not that easy. Sherry.
-Tell her what he did that day.

179
00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:36.576
He messed with the handbrake
on Vincent's car.

180
00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.296
It rolled into the lake.
Totalled.

181
00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:43.960
Well. luckily. Vincent wasn't
in it. but he could have been.

182
00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.376
-Hi.
-Hm?

183
00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.840
-Could I speak with you?
-Of course.

184
00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.056
I overheard
your conversation with Sherry.

185
00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.056
and...

186
00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.440
I just think
someone needs to say it.

187
00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.656
Derek's not a bad kid.
Well. he's misunderstood.

188
00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:12.576
And. I mean. Vincent...

189
00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.656
Vincent upset a lot of people
with that board vote.

190
00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.976
I don't think it's fair that
people go straight to Derek.

191
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.736
If that's what
the police are doing.

192
00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.456
Unfortunately. the police always
take the most direct route.

193
00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:27.576
It... It's good of you
to. er. to speak up for him.

194
00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.680
Yeah.

195
00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:33.216
That vote seems to have frayed
a lot of tempers.

196
00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:34.296
It has.

197
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.336
And...

198
00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:40.536
Sherry insisted on having the
vote when Vincent wasn't there.

199
00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.176
-None of this feels right to me.
-Ah.

200
00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.696
And I feel so bad
for Derek's mother

201
00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.560
coming here every day
with all this happening.

202
00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.760
What about Derek's mum?

203
00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:54.280
-[Fergus] Harry.
-Um... I'll leave you to it.

204
00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.760
-Thank you. again.
-Yeah.

205
00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.280
Everything all right?

206
00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:05.760
Mm.

207
00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.176
That's his first lie exposed.

208
00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.416
Now. he left the form room
that night.

209
00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.896
The lads don't believe
in snitching.

210
00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:17.016
-But they did.
-A man was murdered. Mother.

211
00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.936
Yeah. and why do you want him
to be innocent?

212
00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:20.736
I just want him
to have a fair shot.

213
00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.536
Why do you want him
to be guilty?

214
00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:25.336
-Because he most likely is.
-Oh. I get it.

215
00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.616
He tormented you. but you don't
know anything about his life.

216
00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.056
I think Fergus has a point.
Whatever about his background.

217
00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.296
the kid obviously
has anger issues.

218
00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.336
Well. that doesn't
make him a murderer.

219
00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.416
Look. let's not pretend

220
00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.736
that you didn't grow up in
a nice little bubble. Charlie.

221
00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.160
and despite our problems
with Marcello.

222
00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:46.576
You both have had tough times
in your life.

223
00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.856
but both of you
have had people who loved you.

224
00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:52.016
And you. Fergus. you've had
people who gave you a chance.

225
00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.880
Doesn't Derek deserve a chance?

226
00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.856
No. it's not even remotely
the same thing. Harry.

227
00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.800
-[Skeevie] All right. Happy?
-Don't do that. He's a bully.

228
00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:04.616
I might have a bit of gear that
needs shifting. You interested?

229
00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.000
Nope.

230
00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.696
I'm out of that game now.
Stephen.

231
00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.440
On the straight and narrow.

232
00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:14.576
I had to hear it for meself!

233
00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:18.096
So. Paula has you whipped.

234
00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:19.816
And I've never been happier.

235
00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.056
Oh.

236
00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:23.696
[Malky] Once a toe-rag.

237
00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.496
-always a toe-rag.
-[Fergus sighs] Jesus!

238
00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:29.576
And there's you telling Paula you
are done with the dodgy dealings.

239
00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.816
Now look at you.
chatting to Skeevie.

240
00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:34.320
I'm just having a quiet pint.
Malky.

241
00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:38.016
Maybe go home
and have a coffee. yeah?

242
00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.240
[Skeevie] I'll be off.

243
00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.976
Let's have no trouble.

244
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.856
[door creaks open. closes]

245
00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.680
You're messing her around.

246
00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:50.640
Nope.

247
00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.640
That was you for years.

248
00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.400
And you lost her because of it.

249
00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:01.696
-Hey!
-Jesus!

250
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.040
Whoa. whoa. Malky.
Hey. here. Calm down.

251
00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:10.376
What are you doing?

252
00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:12.736
He's scum.

253
00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:15.240
You've always been scum!

254
00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.536
He's taking your mother
for a ride.

255
00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:23.080
She can look after herself. Da.

256
00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.696
[Charlie] Grab that.

257
00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.456
I'll take him home.

258
00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:30.440
-Oh. oy. oy. There we go.
-Come on.

259
00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.896
That was my dad. growing up.

260
00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.016
And I didn't become a bully.

261
00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.456
People don't change. Harry.

262
00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.840
And I'm telling you.
Derek Robinson hasn't.

263
00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.840
But you don't wanna hear it.

264
00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.136
<i>Hi. this is Jordan.
Leave a message.</i>

265
00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:58.776
-[beep]
-Jordan. I need a favour.

266
00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:01.640
I need to know
about Derek Robinson.

267
00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.880
And I want a contact
for his mum.

268
00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.656
[Harry] Thank you for being
willing to talk with me.

269
00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.456
[woman] I'm happy to talk.

270
00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:13.096
Sorry I have to do it here.
I've got to finish up.

271
00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.096
-I have to get to work.
-I thought this was your work.

272
00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.040
I have a second job.

273
00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.016
You know your son. Derek.

274
00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.536
came to my company
and asked for help?

275
00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:26.360
The police will realise
he did nothing wrong.

276
00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.256
Is that your experience
with the police?

277
00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.840
That they always
get things right?

278
00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:36.576
My colleague doesn't want us
to take this case.

279
00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.096
Derek lied to us already

280
00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.656
about leaving the form room
that night.

281
00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.536
He didn't kill him.

282
00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.696
I promise you that.

283
00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:48.376
Look. my colleague also said that
Derek was trouble in his last school.

284
00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.400
Boys aren't always easy.

285
00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:55.640
And Derek's father...
was especially difficult.

286
00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:59.320
For me and my son.

287
00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:02.976
-Do you have any children?
-I have a son.

288
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.816
-His father?
-Absent.

289
00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.016
-So you know how hard it can be.
-I do.

290
00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:13.096
My boy isn't perfect.
but he has a good heart

291
00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:15.800
and he deserves this chance.

292
00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:20.400
As one mother to another.
will you help him?

293
00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:24.280
I'll do my best.

294
00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:27.216
[Charlie] You left
your form room that night.

295
00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:29.776
-Where did you go?
-Who ratted?

296
00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:32.296
-Oh. answer the question.
-We know you're lying.

297
00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.936
This is stupid.
You sound just like those cops.

298
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.376
I thought you'd help me.

299
00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.176
-Did you kill him?
-No!

300
00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:39.496
It's best you tell the truth. son.

301
00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:41.256
You did. didn't you?

302
00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:44.120
Charlie. Fergus. stop it!
Sit down!

303
00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:47.000
Derek. pick up that chair!

304
00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:50.400
Stop ruining
my bloody furniture.

305
00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.040
Look at me. young man.

306
00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.536
I've met your mum.

307
00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:01.976
She's a good woman.
she works hard.

308
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.536
A woman like that
doesn't raise an idiot.

309
00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.360
even if you choose
to act like one.

310
00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:12.096
[sighs] Look. I've promised her
that I will help you.

311
00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:14.256
so I'm going
to take on this case.

312
00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.840
but we're going to start
with the truth.

313
00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.256
What were you doing
outside your form room

314
00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:23.000
and why didn't you tell us
in the first place?

315
00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:29.120
You're not supposed to leave
after 8:30 on week nights.

316
00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.656
But the school doesn't
pay great.

317
00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.336
so my ma had to take
another job.

318
00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.496
I sneak out and help her clean

319
00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.960
so she can go off
and do offices.

320
00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.936
If the school found out.
they'd probably sack her

321
00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:45.576
and use that as another reason
to throw me out.

322
00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:49.080
I see.
But the pranks you were playing.

323
00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:54.480
Totalling the headmaster's car
seems extreme.

324
00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:57.360
It's hard to explain.

325
00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.480
Well. try.

326
00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:04.536
In me old school.

327
00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:08.016
I made sure people were
too afraid to pick on me.

328
00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.400
[scoffs]

329
00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:13.576
At Bart's.
I thought I could change.

330
00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:18.296
but me accent and me uniform.
being second-hand.

331
00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:20.120
the lads had a pop.

332
00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.576
I knew I couldn't
intimidate them

333
00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:24.816
so I thought
I'd make them like me.

334
00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.936
By being a rebel?

335
00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.176
Why pick on the headmaster?

336
00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:31.320
You must have known
that would be trouble.

337
00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:35.856
He didn't care the other lads
were making things hard for me.

338
00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.760
Quinn only liked rich kids.

339
00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.440
He was the real bully.

340
00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:47.456
[Charlie] He wasn't actually with
his mother at the time of death.

341
00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.896
And even if he was. your
own mother is not a solid alibi.

342
00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.656
I'm not saying he did it!

343
00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.216
I'm just saying sometimes it's
more obvious than you think.

344
00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.816
Go with the evidence.

345
00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.936
[Fergus] We all heard him. OK?
He hated Quinn.

346
00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:01.296
We need to look at that vote
over the land.

347
00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.336
-There's something there.
-And how are we gonna do that?

348
00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.680
Er... I don't know.

349
00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:11.040
Charlie. shouldn't you
be getting home to Orla?

350
00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:14.800
Mm? Oh. yeah. er... fair point.

351
00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:21.640
[front door closes]

352
00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:24.536
What are you up to?

353
00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.560
[bike bell rings]

354
00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:32.416
I could lose my job.
letting you in like this.

355
00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:34.656
Once we get in. you go.

356
00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:37.200
If we get caught.
we won't mention you. I promise.

357
00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.896
Look. I told you on the phone

358
00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:43.040
that we've investigated dozens
of cases and got to the truth.

359
00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.016
I think that Vincent was
murdered because of that vote.

360
00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:50.360
So. if you truly want
to help Derek. help us.

361
00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.376
Yeah.

362
00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.040
[lock turns]

363
00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:57.280
Good luck.

364
00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:05.336
[Harry] Where there's land.
there's money.

365
00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:07.456
Where there's money.
there's greed.

366
00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.336
Yeah. sure.
but what are we looking for?

367
00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:14.576
I don't know. Poisoned letters?
Emails? Brown envelopes?

368
00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:17.736
Yeah. I thought the land was
being sold for the school's benefit.

369
00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:20.056
Aren't they building
affordable homes on it?

370
00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.376
I mean. if no one personally
benefits. if that's the case.

371
00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.280
it's a good thing. right?

372
00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.016
Unless...

373
00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.576
Unless what?

374
00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.880
Unless someone very dodgy
is involved.

375
00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.976
Guess who personally
overturned the Planning Act

376
00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.416
to rezone that land.

377
00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.560
Nicholas bloody Samson.

378
00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:51.376
A woman in a dress like that
shouldn't open her own door.

379
00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.576
Give me a second
to be a gentleman. won't you?

380
00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:57.000
I gave you five seconds.
Then I got impatient.

381
00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.680
[chamber music playing]

382
00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:07.136
I had no idea you were
a patron of this charity.

383
00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.696
Well. you know me.
I like to help the underdog.

384
00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:13.200
I'm not sure I know you at all.
but I'm enjoying getting to.

385
00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.896
Ooh.

386
00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:20.160
-Great speaking with you. Nicholas. Let's talk soon.
-Of course. Good to see you.

387
00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:21.976
[chuckles] Awful man.

388
00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.656
Oh. Ms Wild. isn't it?

389
00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:28.936
So good to see you again.
and such a worthy cause.

390
00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:33.496
It seems we're both invested
in eradicating homelessness.

391
00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:37.296
There's barely a project you haven't
put your personal seal of approval on.

392
00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:41.016
Including. of course.
the protected land at St Bart's?

393
00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:42.776
Sometimes.
tough decisions have to be made.

394
00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.736
It's my job to make sure
that homes are built.

395
00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:47.736
And will these homes
be affordable

396
00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.456
or luxury developments?

397
00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:52.096
I'm confused. Don't you want
people to be housed?

398
00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.576
If so. you're at the wrong
charity event.

399
00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.840
I just want you to know
that I'm still around.

400
00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.240
So I see.

401
00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.736
Did you know Vincent Quinn?

402
00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:06.376
He was the headmaster
at St Bart's. he was murdered.

403
00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:09.056
Strange how these things
keep happening around you.

404
00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.696
What interesting things you say.

405
00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.000
You know. I've been thinking
a lot about you recently.

406
00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.856
Mr Kennedy. I must tell the
Minister for Justice that I saw you.

407
00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:21.800
We're due to review your tenure.
aren't we?

408
00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:24.240
Enjoy your evening.

409
00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:30.336
So. we're not here
for the bad roast dinner.

410
00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:32.336
If he tries to interfere
with your position.

411
00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:34.136
-it'll be my fault.
-Please. Harry.

412
00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.016
I know how to play the game.

413
00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:38.920
But I get the sense
that he doesn't just play.

414
00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:42.096
Think he had
your headmaster killed?

415
00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:44.816
Well. I think they were
on the same side. but...

416
00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.576
if Vince couldn't deliver
the vote.

417
00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.960
I mean Samson's capable
of having him murdered.

418
00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.240
But I don't think
that's what happened.

419
00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:58.056
-That man is Icarus!
-Flying too close to the sun.

420
00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.840
Ah. and I for one can't wait
to watch him burn.

421
00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:06.776
[insistent knocking]

422
00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.800
Oh. keep your pants on!

423
00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.000
Sherry?

424
00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:18.736
[Fergus] What's going on?

425
00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:21.096
The police have been
questioning Arthur.

426
00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:23.296
Arthur hasn't done
anything wrong.

427
00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:26.856
but the board was about to vote
on him becoming permanent head.

428
00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:29.176
I have to abstain
because of our relationship.

429
00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:31.056
but with the police
interrogating him

430
00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:33.216
and me not there
to speak for him...

431
00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:36.056
But why
are they questioning him?

432
00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:40.136
He wasn't with anyone. see?
When Vincent was pushed?

433
00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:42.896
We'd taken the break
from the meeting

434
00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:45.176
and Arthur wanted some air.

435
00:22:45.200 --> 00:22:47.040
I was with the other
board members.

436
00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.416
Well. this could be
a little difficult. Sherry.

437
00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:53.576
We're working to prove
Derek's innocence.

438
00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:56.896
But isn't the most important
thing to get to the truth?

439
00:22:56.920 --> 00:23:00.456
I'm telling you.
Arthur did not kill Vincent.

440
00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:02.176
He's a good man

441
00:23:02.200 --> 00:23:04.896
and he's the best headmaster
that Bart's could have.

442
00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:07.816
Well. for us to get to the bottom
of what happened that night.

443
00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:10.080
I need to be inside the school.

444
00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:13.216
OK?

445
00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:14.856
Oh.

446
00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:18.440
You mean
inside-inside the school.

447
00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:21.256
[Fergus groans]

448
00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:23.016
What?

449
00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:26.936
Some of the other teachers
are aware of why you're here.

450
00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:31.176
but for the most part.
the staff and the student body

451
00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:34.576
believe that you are just
a substitute teacher.

452
00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:38.336
It's very important that the boys'
education doesn't suffer. Ms Wild.

453
00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:41.176
It's Professor Wild.
and can I assure you.

454
00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:44.160
these will be the best
English lessons of their lives.

455
00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:46.440
[phone rings]

456
00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:50.536
If you'll excuse me.
another worried parent.

457
00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.280
Of course.

458
00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:54.240
Ah.

459
00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:01.576
I wasn't expecting this.

460
00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:03.896
Well. the police have started
to look at Arthur

461
00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:05.656
so he was willing to oblige.

462
00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:09.360
This is the best way for me to
figure out what really happened.

463
00:24:10.120 --> 00:24:12.336
Look. I hate to say this.

464
00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:17.000
but Arthur and Sherry do seem
like the most obvious suspects.

465
00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:20.896
They were both vehemently
against Vincent's plan to sell the land.

466
00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:23.416
Unfortunately. for the police.
that's still Derek.

467
00:24:23.440 --> 00:24:25.640
He has a bit of a reputation
with them.

468
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:29.136
And he was a bully
in his last school.

469
00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:32.776
He was a bully?
I didn't know that.

470
00:24:32.800 --> 00:24:34.976
Well. that doesn't make him
a killer.

471
00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:37.560
Oh. but it's still a surprise.

472
00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:41.376
Would you... Would you like me
to show you around?

473
00:24:41.400 --> 00:24:43.176
That would be lovely.

474
00:24:43.200 --> 00:24:44.480
Yeah.

475
00:24:46.200 --> 00:24:49.960
-[Harry] Very impressive!
-Oh. we do OK.

476
00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:53.456
-Ooh! Percival D'arcy.
-[self-effacing laugh]

477
00:24:53.480 --> 00:24:54.776
Chess champion.

478
00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:56.656
-You were a student here?
-Yes. yeah.

479
00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:58.296
And now you teach here.

480
00:24:58.320 --> 00:25:00.616
Yeah. well. some would call it
Stockholm Syndrome.

481
00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:03.536
[chuckles] Nine years ago.

482
00:25:03.560 --> 00:25:05.576
Vincent was your headmaster!

483
00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:09.416
Yes. he's the reason that
I came back. He was a great man

484
00:25:09.440 --> 00:25:13.776
and. well. I was honoured when
he accepted me for the position.

485
00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:17.216
I heard that his favourites
were always the rich boys.

486
00:25:17.240 --> 00:25:20.576
-You must come from money.
-[uncomfortable laugh]

487
00:25:20.600 --> 00:25:23.216
Well. the first rule
of money club

488
00:25:23.240 --> 00:25:25.320
is that we don't talk
about money club.

489
00:25:25.800 --> 00:25:27.576
-[chuckles]
-Shall we?

490
00:25:27.600 --> 00:25:29.040
Yes.

491
00:25:31.680 --> 00:25:35.496
This year's reading list
is very male heavy.

492
00:25:35.520 --> 00:25:39.936
<i>East of Eden. Nicholas Nickleby.
Ulysses.</i> Ugh!

493
00:25:39.960 --> 00:25:41.936
So. let's shake it up. shall we?

494
00:25:41.960 --> 00:25:47.656
How about some Woolf?
Or Harper Lee? Or the Brontes?

495
00:25:47.680 --> 00:25:52.136
-My father calls that chick-lit.
-[students laughs]

496
00:25:52.160 --> 00:25:55.816
The Brontes were
literary geniuses.

497
00:25:55.840 --> 00:25:58.216
They were so far ahead
of their time

498
00:25:58.240 --> 00:26:01.096
that their writings
are still considered feminist.

499
00:26:01.120 --> 00:26:03.656
politically
and racially astute today.

500
00:26:03.680 --> 00:26:06.216
And all of that

501
00:26:06.240 --> 00:26:08.896
while living a very sheltered
life in a parsonage.

502
00:26:08.920 --> 00:26:10.736
never ever seeing the world!

503
00:26:10.760 --> 00:26:14.000
-So. they were bored chicks.
-[laughter]

504
00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:17.296
No one with a brain
is ever bored.

505
00:26:17.320 --> 00:26:19.976
Their lives were very difficult.

506
00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.496
Almost half the population
of their village

507
00:26:22.520 --> 00:26:24.456
died before the age of six.

508
00:26:24.480 --> 00:26:27.960
The sisters themselves
all died young.

509
00:26:28.840 --> 00:26:33.296
Many historians now believe that
most of the village of Haworth

510
00:26:33.320 --> 00:26:38.160
was drinking water that was
contaminated by the graveyard.

511
00:26:38.800 --> 00:26:40.496
[students] Eugh!

512
00:26:40.520 --> 00:26:43.416
Well. poverty and hardship
wasn't their only challenge.

513
00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:47.776
The sisters had to use
male pen-names to get published.

514
00:26:47.800 --> 00:26:52.320
Because. of course. the world
was dominated by stupid men.

515
00:26:53.240 --> 00:26:57.776
And going by your
and your father's opinion.

516
00:26:57.800 --> 00:26:59.176
not much has changed.

517
00:26:59.200 --> 00:27:02.816
-[students] Ooh!
-[laughter]

518
00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:07.496
So. shall we ditch
the navel-gazing of <i>Ulysses</i>

519
00:27:07.520 --> 00:27:11.936
and visit the mad woman in the
attic of <i>Jane Eyre.</i> shall we?

520
00:27:11.960 --> 00:27:13.960
[knock on window]

521
00:27:18.800 --> 00:27:21.216
How did the police
miss evidence?

522
00:27:21.240 --> 00:27:22.856
I don't know.

523
00:27:22.880 --> 00:27:26.016
but Vicky told Charlie
that they've found something

524
00:27:26.040 --> 00:27:28.240
and they believe
it's significant.

525
00:27:29.680 --> 00:27:32.696
They've taken some of these
blue chips as evidence.

526
00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:35.776
It's like the killer
put his foot up. like this.

527
00:27:35.800 --> 00:27:38.856
And used it as leverage
to push Vincent over?

528
00:27:38.880 --> 00:27:40.736
Yeah.

529
00:27:40.760 --> 00:27:43.440
Do the police know
where the blue paint came from?

530
00:27:56.680 --> 00:27:58.360
Mm-hm.

531
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:03.296
Some people might feel this way
about Yeats

532
00:28:03.320 --> 00:28:06.040
but I. for one. have always
found him fascinating.

533
00:28:07.120 --> 00:28:10.176
"An aged man
is but a paltry thing.

534
00:28:10.200 --> 00:28:13.016
a tattered coat upon a stick."

535
00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:16.136
But wait. perhaps this isn't
your reflection on the poetry.

536
00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:19.360
It's a... self-portrait?

537
00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:22.440
[laughter]

538
00:28:24.200 --> 00:28:27.040
Less arse. more art.

539
00:28:30.440 --> 00:28:31.640
Hm.

540
00:28:35.160 --> 00:28:38.896
"Yeats. a man willing to examine
and eviscerate himself

541
00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:41.616
at every turn without fear
or censorship.

542
00:28:41.640 --> 00:28:44.800
to give of himself
these glorious words."

543
00:28:46.680 --> 00:28:48.776
This is beautiful.
What's your name?

544
00:28:48.800 --> 00:28:50.256
Peter. Miss.

545
00:28:50.280 --> 00:28:52.216
Alexander. you should read
Peter's essay.

546
00:28:52.240 --> 00:28:55.576
-You might learn something.
-I don't need to read his essay.

547
00:28:55.600 --> 00:28:58.216
Headmaster Quinn
personally chose me

548
00:28:58.240 --> 00:29:00.296
for the annual
essay-writing competition.

549
00:29:00.320 --> 00:29:03.240
Did the headmaster
ever comment on your work?

550
00:29:04.960 --> 00:29:07.816
Well. you're the one that should
be submitting your work

551
00:29:07.840 --> 00:29:09.256
for that competition.

552
00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:11.440
You have a way with words.

553
00:29:16.840 --> 00:29:18.176
-Ssh!
-[laughter]

554
00:29:18.200 --> 00:29:20.776
[school bell rings]

555
00:29:20.800 --> 00:29:23.056
[Harry] I am getting
the distinct impression

556
00:29:23.080 --> 00:29:25.880
that Vincent wasn't
the fairest of headmasters.

557
00:29:26.920 --> 00:29:29.400
Telling me the truth won't
make me think you're guilty.

558
00:29:30.920 --> 00:29:33.736
Vincent could be narrow-sighted.

559
00:29:33.760 --> 00:29:37.216
He thought that some boys needed
more pressure than others.

560
00:29:37.240 --> 00:29:39.096
Let me guess. the poor ones?

561
00:29:39.120 --> 00:29:41.640
-Huh.
-Was he a bully?

562
00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:46.016
Did he torment Derek
or the other kids?

563
00:29:46.040 --> 00:29:48.696
Well. that's the problem.

564
00:29:48.720 --> 00:29:52.376
If he was doing something outright.
something you could put your finger on.

565
00:29:52.400 --> 00:29:54.016
But he wasn't.

566
00:29:54.040 --> 00:29:56.016
And there are many boys
and teachers

567
00:29:56.040 --> 00:29:58.296
and parents associated
with this school

568
00:29:58.320 --> 00:30:00.576
who feel that Vincent
was a brilliant head.

569
00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:03.616
That just means
he was a clever bully. Arthur.

570
00:30:03.640 --> 00:30:06.960
and nobody here
was willing to catch him out.

571
00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:11.080
I guess you're right.

572
00:30:13.680 --> 00:30:15.600
[phone buzzes]

573
00:30:18.040 --> 00:30:19.576
Hello?

574
00:30:19.600 --> 00:30:21.656
[distorted voice]
<i>Back off. you stupid bitch.</i>

575
00:30:21.680 --> 00:30:25.216
<i>-That cape fools nobody.</i>
-Who is this?

576
00:30:25.240 --> 00:30:27.896
<i>You're not even a real teacher.</i>

577
00:30:27.920 --> 00:30:30.496
<i>Keep asking questions
and see what happens to you.</i>

578
00:30:30.520 --> 00:30:32.496
[call ends]

579
00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:33.840
[beep]

580
00:30:39.160 --> 00:30:41.656
I'm fine. it takes more than
that to scare me.

581
00:30:41.680 --> 00:30:44.296
[Fergus] <i>Look. you're obviously
asking the right questions.</i>

582
00:30:44.320 --> 00:30:46.536
<i>but I'm not sure about you being
in there on your own. Harry.</i>

583
00:30:46.560 --> 00:30:50.256
Well. what are you suggesting?
We smuggle you in as a student?

584
00:30:50.280 --> 00:30:52.216
<i>Hell. no!</i>

585
00:30:52.240 --> 00:30:54.776
<i>I had enough of real school.
I'm barely able for lectures.</i>

586
00:30:54.800 --> 00:30:57.360
[unclear banter]

587
00:30:57.920 --> 00:31:00.416
I have to call you back. Fergus.

588
00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:02.456
If you're going to get a pair of fake trainers.
at least get a pair that can pass muster.

589
00:31:02.480 --> 00:31:05.296
-Just give it a rest. Tobias.
-Do what your master says. will ya?

590
00:31:05.320 --> 00:31:07.896
-I'm just trying to help out. pal.
-Pal? I'm not your pal.

591
00:31:07.920 --> 00:31:11.536
I can't stay here. mate. What makes
you think you can speak to me like that?

592
00:31:11.560 --> 00:31:15.200
-What? Speak to you like what...
-Everything OK here?

593
00:31:16.680 --> 00:31:18.840
Just messing around. miss.

594
00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:24.800
Well. try messing around
with someone else.

595
00:31:48.680 --> 00:31:50.640
[floorboards creak]

596
00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:57.040
[tense music]

597
00:32:05.960 --> 00:32:07.440
Ooh!

598
00:32:09.280 --> 00:32:10.976
Hello?

599
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:12.600
Hello!

600
00:32:13.720 --> 00:32:15.200
Hello!

601
00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:35.136
Really. Ma? You're doing
undercover work now?

602
00:32:35.160 --> 00:32:38.296
Keep up. I've done it loads. it
works and I'm learning things.

603
00:32:38.320 --> 00:32:40.256
Yeah. like how to get locked in.

604
00:32:40.280 --> 00:32:42.456
You can't stay here. If you're
right and Derek didn't do this...

605
00:32:42.480 --> 00:32:43.936
I'm right.

606
00:32:43.960 --> 00:32:45.936
Then the real killer
is obviously onto you.

607
00:32:45.960 --> 00:32:48.816
Oh. number one.
I am staying here. Number two.

608
00:32:48.840 --> 00:32:50.936
take out both your phones.

609
00:32:50.960 --> 00:32:54.440
Specifically. the photographs
of the crime scene.

610
00:32:57.560 --> 00:32:59.576
Is that from the first set
that Jordan sent?

611
00:32:59.600 --> 00:33:01.096
Yes.

612
00:33:01.120 --> 00:33:03.016
Fergus. I need the second set
that Jordan sent.

613
00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:05.920
the one you showed me
with the paint on the rail.

614
00:33:06.520 --> 00:33:08.160
-Here.
-Hm.

615
00:33:10.160 --> 00:33:11.896
That paint wasn't there

616
00:33:11.920 --> 00:33:14.216
when they first examined
the crime scene.

617
00:33:14.240 --> 00:33:17.160
-Somebody put it there.
-Shit! Why?

618
00:33:18.120 --> 00:33:21.840
To frame Derek Robinson.
Those were his shoes.

619
00:33:23.360 --> 00:33:26.160
You need to let Jordan know
this is a ploy.

620
00:33:27.040 --> 00:33:29.640
[phone beeps. ringing]

621
00:33:31.840 --> 00:33:35.000
-Hup.
-[Harry] Excuse me?

622
00:33:40.080 --> 00:33:44.456
I. er. I believe you're the boys
that told this gentleman

623
00:33:44.480 --> 00:33:48.456
that Derek left his form room the night
that your headmaster was murdered?

624
00:33:48.480 --> 00:33:50.896
-Yeah.
-And?

625
00:33:50.920 --> 00:33:53.416
Well. and you drew attention

626
00:33:53.440 --> 00:33:55.696
to the fact that his trainers
were fake

627
00:33:55.720 --> 00:33:57.616
and there was blue paint
coming off of them.

628
00:33:57.640 --> 00:33:59.336
Yeah. so what?

629
00:33:59.360 --> 00:34:02.160
Well. it's almost like
you want him to be in trouble.

630
00:34:03.080 --> 00:34:05.840
We shouldn't have to go
to a school with kids like that.

631
00:34:06.640 --> 00:34:09.856
Do you know how much my father
pays for me to go here?

632
00:34:09.880 --> 00:34:12.856
I think the relevant information
there is that it's your father paying.

633
00:34:12.880 --> 00:34:17.240
-Excuse me. but who are you?
-OK. Tobias. mate... chill.

634
00:34:19.200 --> 00:34:21.776
We're sorry about that.
We're just kidding.

635
00:34:21.800 --> 00:34:24.416
We understand
how serious all of this is.

636
00:34:24.440 --> 00:34:27.056
I'm glad to hear that.

637
00:34:27.080 --> 00:34:29.856
So. did the police
ask you any questions

638
00:34:29.880 --> 00:34:32.880
about where you were
the night your headmaster died?

639
00:34:34.440 --> 00:34:37.400
Oh. our... our parents wouldn't
allow us to be questioned.

640
00:34:39.800 --> 00:34:43.240
It's crazy. that. We liked him.

641
00:34:44.800 --> 00:34:47.816
We could have just
pushed him off for fun.

642
00:34:47.840 --> 00:34:50.480
and made sure Derek
took the blame.

643
00:34:51.760 --> 00:34:54.856
[both laugh out loud]

644
00:34:54.880 --> 00:34:57.920
But of course we'd never
do that. but if we did...

645
00:34:59.040 --> 00:35:02.760
If we did. our parents would make
sure we were never held to account.

646
00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:08.696
I'm sure you'll find that Mummy
and Daddy can only do so much.

647
00:35:08.720 --> 00:35:11.136
Money doesn't buy you
everything.

648
00:35:11.160 --> 00:35:13.976
It'll buy us futures
outside of this place.

649
00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:16.936
We won't be stuck like those
paupers who end up working here.

650
00:35:16.960 --> 00:35:20.936
-What paupers?
-The scholarship kids.

651
00:35:20.960 --> 00:35:23.256
They all end up teaching here
in the end.

652
00:35:23.280 --> 00:35:25.216
Nowhere else will have them.

653
00:35:25.240 --> 00:35:27.216
Which teachers?

654
00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:28.856
-Half of them.
-Mm.

655
00:35:28.880 --> 00:35:30.776
-D'arcy. Rowe.
-Yeah.

656
00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:33.056
-Mr Loomes.
-[both snigger]

657
00:35:33.080 --> 00:35:37.640
What's it they say?
"Those who can't do. teach."

658
00:35:39.680 --> 00:35:42.760
You could say the same for those
who come here on scholarships.

659
00:35:44.160 --> 00:35:46.240
I mean. it's true. isn't it?

660
00:35:54.640 --> 00:35:56.696
You know.
I never thought I'd say this.

661
00:35:56.720 --> 00:35:58.776
but I really hope
you're right about Derek

662
00:35:58.800 --> 00:36:01.136
and it's one of those two
who go down.

663
00:36:01.160 --> 00:36:03.776
All right. Harry?
You still with me?

664
00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:06.440
Oh. sorry.
I have to go to class.

665
00:36:06.880 --> 00:36:10.160
I promised Arthur that I'd give
these boys an education.

666
00:36:10.880 --> 00:36:12.560
I've got to go.

667
00:36:13.320 --> 00:36:15.440
OK. Bye so?

668
00:36:16.600 --> 00:36:18.656
Guess I'll make my own way out.

669
00:36:18.680 --> 00:36:21.056
[Harry] "'Sit down. beggar!'"

670
00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:23.856
screamed Squeers.
almost beside himself with rage

671
00:36:23.880 --> 00:36:26.600
and seizing Smike as he spoke.

672
00:36:27.360 --> 00:36:30.496
'Wretch. ' rejoined Nicholas. fiercely.

673
00:36:30.520 --> 00:36:31.936
'Touch him at your peril!

674
00:36:31.960 --> 00:36:34.016
I will not stand by.
and see it done.

675
00:36:34.040 --> 00:36:37.896
My blood is up. and I have the
strength of ten such men as you.

676
00:36:37.920 --> 00:36:40.536
Look to yourself. for Heaven
I will not spare you.

677
00:36:40.560 --> 00:36:42.560
if you drive me on!'

678
00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:46.880
'Stand back. ' cried Squeers.
brandishing his weapon.

679
00:36:47.760 --> 00:36:50.216
'I have a long series of insults
to avenge. '

680
00:36:50.240 --> 00:36:52.336
said Nicholas.
flushed with passion.

681
00:36:52.360 --> 00:36:54.176
'and my indignation
is aggravated

682
00:36:54.200 --> 00:36:56.176
by the dastardly cruelties
practised

683
00:36:56.200 --> 00:36:59.040
on helpless infancy
in this foul den.

684
00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:01.416
Have a care;

685
00:37:01.440 --> 00:37:03.856
for if you do raise
the devil within me.

686
00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:07.640
"the consequences shall fall
heavily upon your own head.'"

687
00:37:12.720 --> 00:37:15.896
Fergus. I think I know what
happened. but I need evidence.

688
00:37:15.920 --> 00:37:18.800
And get Charlie. We need a plan.

689
00:37:20.240 --> 00:37:22.736
[Jordan] I just wanted
to update you all

690
00:37:22.760 --> 00:37:24.496
on the current state
of the case.

691
00:37:24.520 --> 00:37:26.496
Now. as you may know.
we found what we believed to be

692
00:37:26.520 --> 00:37:28.696
some evidence
where Mr Quinn was pushed.

693
00:37:28.720 --> 00:37:31.576
However. the Director
of Public Prosecutions

694
00:37:31.600 --> 00:37:35.216
doesn't believe it's substantial
enough to issue a warrant.

695
00:37:35.240 --> 00:37:38.616
We're now considering the land
sale as the primary motive.

696
00:37:38.640 --> 00:37:41.136
That is nonsense.
We all know who did this.

697
00:37:41.160 --> 00:37:42.856
When are you going
to arrest him?

698
00:37:42.880 --> 00:37:46.216
-Sherry!
-There is a strong suspect.

699
00:37:46.240 --> 00:37:47.856
but we need more evidence

700
00:37:47.880 --> 00:37:50.496
and for now. we have to keep
our options open.

701
00:37:50.520 --> 00:37:54.160
Mr Rowe. I wanted to reinterview
you. if that's all right.

702
00:38:01.640 --> 00:38:03.336
You're meant to be helping him.

703
00:38:03.360 --> 00:38:05.576
It's obvious
that Derek did this.

704
00:38:05.600 --> 00:38:08.440
And it's obvious
that they need proof.

705
00:38:08.840 --> 00:38:10.040
[huffs]

706
00:38:39.240 --> 00:38:41.176
Caught in the act.

707
00:38:41.200 --> 00:38:42.840
Percival.

708
00:38:44.080 --> 00:38:48.296
Planting evidence
that only the killer could have.

709
00:38:48.320 --> 00:38:51.136
I presume you took these
as security.

710
00:38:51.160 --> 00:38:52.976
in case you needed
to frame somebody.

711
00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:55.096
-[Percival] This is a mistake.
-The mistake's not realising

712
00:38:55.120 --> 00:38:57.776
we searched your room earlier
and discovered these glasses.

713
00:38:57.800 --> 00:39:00.336
owned by the victim.
but we left them in place

714
00:39:00.360 --> 00:39:03.136
so that you could do exactly
what you just tried to do.

715
00:39:03.160 --> 00:39:05.816
Nicholas Nickleby.
that's when I realised.

716
00:39:05.840 --> 00:39:08.256
You were a scholarship
student here.

717
00:39:08.280 --> 00:39:09.896
but you were bullied by Vincent.

718
00:39:09.920 --> 00:39:11.896
You didn't come here
because of Stockholm Syndrome.

719
00:39:11.920 --> 00:39:14.856
You came here
because you wanted revenge.

720
00:39:14.880 --> 00:39:17.136
And you didn't know
how to go about it.

721
00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:20.856
But then you saw Vincent picking
on other kids. especially Derek.

722
00:39:20.880 --> 00:39:22.856
That day. Derek pulled
the prank of all pranks.

723
00:39:22.880 --> 00:39:25.656
totalling Vincent's car.
and Vincent lost it.

724
00:39:25.680 --> 00:39:29.576
And you saw the equivalent of
the cruel headmaster in Nickleby

725
00:39:29.600 --> 00:39:33.736
caning Smike.
and something in you snapped.

726
00:39:33.760 --> 00:39:36.816
I did this to help Derek
and all the others.

727
00:39:36.840 --> 00:39:39.320
This was self-defence.
I... I swear.

728
00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:42.296
Vincent made my life hell when
he started here as headmaster.

729
00:39:42.320 --> 00:39:44.776
But why let Derek
take the blame?

730
00:39:44.800 --> 00:39:47.496
Well. I hadn't planned to but then when I
found out he was a bully in his last school.

731
00:39:47.520 --> 00:39:48.976
he was no better
than the others.

732
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:52.976
Everybody in life
has been bullied. Percival.

733
00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.176
But if you'd just lashed out
at yours.

734
00:39:55.200 --> 00:39:57.880
this would seem understandable.

735
00:39:58.760 --> 00:40:00.680
But to frame a child?

736
00:40:01.960 --> 00:40:05.136
You're the one
that's no better than Vincent.

737
00:40:05.160 --> 00:40:07.136
What the hell would you know?

738
00:40:07.160 --> 00:40:09.536
With your plummy accent
and your fancy college job!

739
00:40:09.560 --> 00:40:12.056
You've no idea
what I've overcome.

740
00:40:12.080 --> 00:40:14.040
-[sirens approaching]
-No idea!

741
00:40:14.760 --> 00:40:17.056
-[handcuffs click]
-Stupid bitch!

742
00:40:17.080 --> 00:40:20.440
-You should have stayed away when I warned you...
-That'll do!

743
00:40:21.840 --> 00:40:23.280
Come on.

744
00:40:27.200 --> 00:40:28.840
[owl hoots]

745
00:40:33.760 --> 00:40:36.496
Me ma wanted to say
thanks as well.

746
00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:39.280
Well. you're very welcome.
You both are.

747
00:40:39.760 --> 00:40:42.016
And I wanted to say sorry for...

748
00:40:42.040 --> 00:40:45.560
you know.
being a little git in school.

749
00:40:46.840 --> 00:40:48.616
Don't worry about it. pal.

750
00:40:48.640 --> 00:40:50.480
Plus. you were never little.

751
00:40:51.040 --> 00:40:53.040
-[chuckles]
-I mean it.

752
00:40:54.040 --> 00:40:55.936
From the bottom of my heart.

753
00:40:55.960 --> 00:40:58.336
There's not many people
that stuck up for Derek.

754
00:40:58.360 --> 00:41:01.240
-I wish we could pay you back.
-He can.

755
00:41:02.400 --> 00:41:05.280
Do brilliantly in your life.
Derek. I'll be watching.

756
00:41:05.920 --> 00:41:07.616
Not sure if they'll let me stay.

757
00:41:07.640 --> 00:41:09.280
Ah. they will.

758
00:41:10.080 --> 00:41:12.440
Just make them see
that it's worth it. yeah?

759
00:41:13.440 --> 00:41:15.200
[Arthur] Derek?

760
00:41:19.480 --> 00:41:22.936
OK. I'm sorry.
You were right about him.

761
00:41:22.960 --> 00:41:25.976
-I'm always right.
-And yet you liked Percival.

762
00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:27.856
-Didn't you?
-Oh. no. not at all.

763
00:41:27.880 --> 00:41:30.160
-I found him intolerable.
-[laughs]

764
00:41:33.200 --> 00:41:36.880
-Time to rain on their parade.
-Oh. absolutely.

765
00:41:41.480 --> 00:41:44.976
Told you. it's always the scholarship
ones that cause the problems.

766
00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:48.440
Not quite.
Not your problems. anyway.

767
00:41:49.240 --> 00:41:50.536
What problems?

768
00:41:50.560 --> 00:41:53.216
Oh. we had a few hours
to kill earlier.

769
00:41:53.240 --> 00:41:56.016
[Harry] And we were
very productive with our time.

770
00:41:56.040 --> 00:42:00.096
We passed every one of your
essays through an AI check.

771
00:42:00.120 --> 00:42:03.096
[Fergus] Turns out. you've been
cheating for a whole year.

772
00:42:03.120 --> 00:42:04.736
Mm. your headmaster is furious.

773
00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:08.896
He wants you to rewrite
everything before the exams.

774
00:42:08.920 --> 00:42:12.000
Which are in three weeks. right?

775
00:42:13.400 --> 00:42:16.800
Mummy and Daddy can't get you
out of this one.

776
00:42:20.840 --> 00:42:22.536
[Harry] I'm proud of you.
Fergus.

777
00:42:22.560 --> 00:42:25.496
It takes a lot of strength
to let go of old grievances.

778
00:42:25.520 --> 00:42:28.736
Yeah. well. I still wouldn't
want to meet him in a dark alley.

779
00:42:28.760 --> 00:42:31.296
I wouldn't want to meet anyone
in a dark alley.

780
00:42:31.320 --> 00:42:33.976
I meet some of best contacts
in dark alleys.

781
00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:35.216
[Charlie laughs]

782
00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:38.936
-You OK?
-Absolutely.

783
00:42:38.960 --> 00:42:40.616
I just need to make
a quick call.

784
00:42:40.640 --> 00:42:43.576
And afterwards.
may I take you out for dinner?

785
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:46.416
-Oh. it's my turn.
-Mm. like I said.

786
00:42:46.440 --> 00:42:49.016
let me be a gentleman
for a second?

787
00:42:49.040 --> 00:42:52.536
OK. OK. you can treat me.

788
00:42:52.560 --> 00:42:54.080
All right.

789
00:42:58.280 --> 00:43:00.256
[Fergus] Well. you look
very happy.

790
00:43:00.280 --> 00:43:01.776
I am.

791
00:43:01.800 --> 00:43:03.600
Very much so.

792
00:43:04.280 --> 00:43:06.400
[theme music]
